          deepDive: "**〜はもとより** is the formal twin of **〜はもちろん** (N3). もとより is an old adverb meaning *from the beginning, as a matter of course*, so AはもとよりBも = *A goes without saying, and B too*. The book: used in speeches and presentations to say \"not only ~ (which is obvious) but other things as well.\"\n\nStructure: **A はもとより、B も / B まで / B にも**. A is the obvious case; B is the one the listener might not expect, or the one you want to add. The order matters: この温泉は、日本人はもとより、外国人にもたいへん人気があります (*it's very popular with foreigners too, not to mention Japanese people*). Swapping A and B makes the less obvious case sound like the given one.\n\nThe second half usually contains **も** (or まで, さえ): 睡眠や運動にも気をつけて, 大企業にとっても, 南米の国々でも. Without a も-type word the sentence feels unfinished. A and B are the same kind of thing (two places, groups, tasks).\n\nRegister: はもちろん is fine in conversation; はもとより sounds like a speech, presentation, brochure or formal writing. In the farewell speech it lists what the speaker learned elegantly: 仕事の進め方はもとより、取引先との付き合い方など… (*how to go about the work, of course, and also how to deal with clients…*).\n\nCompare with close neighbors:\n- **〜はもちろん**: same meaning, everyday register.\n- **〜のみならず** (#63): *not only… but also*, formal, focused on extending the scope without the \"obviously\" feeling: 日本のみならず世界の問題だ (*a problem not only for Japan but for the world*).\n- **〜に限らず** (#72): *not limited to ~* — denies that A is the only case.\n- **〜に加えて** (#136): *in addition to ~* — simply adds B: 雨に加えて風も強くなった (*on top of the rain, the wind picked up*).\n- **〜をはじめ** (#10): names the representative member of a larger group rather than two separate items.\n- **〜ばかりでなく / だけでなく**: neutral *not only*.\n\nTraps in the practice:\n- **に限り** (#3): *only* — the opposite idea: 事前に予約した場合に限り無料で参加できます (*it's free only if you book in advance*).\n- **のもとで** (#11): *under*: 家族のもとで生活しながら (*while living under their family's care*).\n- **においては** (#6) / **にもかかわらず** (#21) don't add a second item, so they can't fill 日本（　）いろいろな国で or スペイン（　）南米の国々でも.\n\nもとより alone is also an adverb: もとより承知しております (*I've been aware of that from the start*).\n\nJLPT tip: if the second half has も / まで / さえ and the item before the blank is the obvious case, はもとより (or はもちろん) is the answer. In 問題2: 宇宙飛行士を目指すからには、体力はもとより、判断力や問題解決能力もきたえておかなければならない (*if you aim to be an astronaut, you must train your judgment and problem-solving, not to mention your stamina*).",
